  - UniversalPersistedPromotedProfileProjection
  - UniversalPersistedPromotedProfileProvenanceService
- tests/FFPerformanceEngine.Core.SelfTest/PersistedPromotedProfileProvenanceSelfTests.cs
- tests/FFPerformanceEngine.Core.SelfTest/Program.cs registration

Fail-closed gates
- exactly one requested persisted generated winner
- winner must be one of five winner roles and Validated
- exact SourceComparisonId, FF/FFMAX game, instance and environment fingerprint
- exactly one parseable receipt claiming the promoted winner
- exact target role and revalidation id correlation
- non-empty/distinct challenger, previous-winner, promoted-winner and revalidation ids
- exact persisted Custom + Validated challenger, same game/instance
- exact persisted revalidation comparison
- baseline and candidate Measured
- structurally equivalent revalidation environments and current structural compatibility
- candidate configuration exact match to Custom and promoted winner, including DPI
- winner and Custom fingerprints equal exact candidate environment id
- winner FPS, 1% low, frame time and latency equal exact revalidation candidate evidence
- current Custom provenance must still re-prove through UniversalValidatedProfileProvenanceService/current candidate-space/current allow-list
- duplicate/missing receipt, missing comparison/capability, phantom winner or any drift => null

Authority boundary
The service never reconstructs ProfileChallengeResult, never re-evaluates the historical two-round challenge verdict, never promotes a profile, never mutates or persists state, and never converts receipt metadata into specialized authority. It transports only the exact universal candidate/identity/adapter already re-proven for the preserved Custom source.

